Thanks for the replies.  I think my main problems with Archons is that
my characters who hit the endgame have been melee-light and largely
rely on magic to dispatch enemies.  A fast, two-weapon valkyrie with a
+7 Frostbane and +7 silver saber is likely to be able to melee an
Archon to death before it summons more than one horde of monsters.  On
the other hand, it was likely to take me 15 hits to kill an Archon or
monster of similar power with just the +6 Magicbane, and that combined
with its stunning effect and the fact that they tend to back off when
injured (while still summoning hordes) makes even blindfolded killing
hard, not to mention just hoping for a unicorn horn to allow me to get
a few hits in.  That's what tanked my last character who made it to the
plane of Fire - he'd jumped through the portal on Air, escaping about
50 summoned monsters, but it seemed a few of them hopped through the
portal along with him, including an Archon (or one was present on
Fire).

Fortunately, on this run I didn't even have to use my potions of full
healing.  Quite a relief.


